Overlay patch 0044: stereoscopic eye rendering for visionOS 3D
(= reference 0031 rev11; VISION-PRO-LUS-PLAYBOOK §2.4/§2.5).
The shell's CompositorServices loop (SohImmersive.m) composites two per-eye
Metal textures onto a world-locked panel. This patch makes Fast3D produce
them: in 3D mode (gSoh3DMode, shell-owned), Fast3dWindow runs the
interpreter TWICE per host frame — same game time, same command list — with
an eye state that (a) swaps mGameFb to a per-eye framebuffer (all existing
offscreen plumbing targets it transparently), and (b) applies an off-axis
stereo projection to PERSPECTIVE matrices only, folded in the CAMERA basis
exported by 0045 (MK64 kart camera). fb 0 (the hidden window's drawable) is
never touched in 3D; EndFrameOffscreen commits the drawn framebuffers,
rides 0021's pending-mip pass, publishes eye textures ON GPU COMPLETION
(double-buffered per eye — the compositor blit-copies with no cross-queue
fence), and replicates EndFrame's state cleanup. Menu/HUD composite into
the eyes via 0043's Gui split. Adaptive convergence: sep = Depth% x conv,
conv smoothed from the exported camera distance.
Port deltas vs reference 0031 (audit + spec 2026-07-22):
- Context::GetRawInstance() -> GetInstance() (our fork has only the
  shared_ptr accessor; both in Soh3DSetEye and the Fast3dWindow anchor).
- E8 SSAA gate: our 0035 SSAA block scales mCurDimensions at the top of
  StartFrame with a default of 2.0 (reference: 1.0) — during an eye pass it
  must not run, or the eye framebuffer is destroyed/recreated twice per
  frame (pre-override resize then override resize; the Ship of Harkinian port survived
  by numeric coincidence at ssaa=1.0). Gate reads sSoh3DEye.
- EndFrameOffscreen additionally attaches our 0027 gpu-ms completion
  handler to the last committed CB so the perf probe stays honest in 3D
  (reference's freezes there; deliberate delta).
- MK64 convergence clamp/fallback kept at reference values [30,3000]/300
  pending live gSoh3DCamDist measurement (MK64 world scale is smaller —
  bridge `3d` reports camDist; retune constants against it on sim).
NOT replicated in EndFrameOffscreen (upstream-only machinery, dormant in
3D): the mScreenReadbackRequested fb-0 deferred-readback path — MK64's
only G_READFB emitter reads a custom fb via the synchronous compute path,
and fb-0 CopyFrameBuffer sources redirect to mGameFb when mRendersToFb.
VR additions (R1, VR-spec D2/D6/D7, all gated on gSohVRWorldActive so the
flat and 3D-panel paths are byte-identical when it is 0):
- Eye-matrix hook: in VR world frames Soh3DStereoP substitutes the shell's
  composed A*V*P eye matrix for the game's combined view*projection. The pose
  is acquired ONCE per host frame (Soh3DSetEye(1) -> SohIosVR_AcquireEyes)
  and its frame id rides back out with the eye texture (Soh3DPublishOnComplete
  tag) so the loop submits the anchor the frame was rendered against (B1).
  This hook lives INSIDE text 0044 inserts, so it lands as a regeneration of
  0044 rather than a stacked patch (R0 structural finding).
- Depth handoff: the eye framebuffer's DEPTH texture is published alongside
  its colour texture, for the loop's forward-Z -> reverse-Z conversion (D2 as
  amended: the compositor is reverse-Z/infinite-far, the engine is not).
- HUD framebuffer: MK64's HUD is RDP texrects that never touch MP_matrix (R0
  finding 2), so the 2D stretch of the display list is redirected into a
  dedicated framebuffer (Soh3DVRTarget, upstream's own mid-list target-switch
  recipe) and composited by the shell as a plane in player space. The sky
  stretch (0046 sentinels) is parked in the same framebuffer and wiped, which
  is how R1 "skips the sky in VR".
- Alpha-0 clears: eye + HUD framebuffers clear to alpha 0 while VR world
  frames are active, so .mixed shows the room around the diorama.
VR R3 additions (rev3, spec D12 — the rear-view pane):
- A THIRD interpreter walk, eye index 3, run ONLY while the shell says the
  pane is visible (gSohVRMirrorActive). It renders into its own small mono
  framebuffer (gSohVRMirrorW/H, ~half the eye extent per axis) which is
  published on GPU completion exactly like the eyes and the HUD.
- The mirror matrix is NOT hand-rolled and needs no shell publish: the pass
  reuses the GAME's own combined view*projection and pre-multiplies a world
  transform that rotates 180 degrees about the vertical axis through the KART
  (camEye + camFwd*camDist, 0045's export). Rotating the world about the kart
  and keeping the camera is exactly "a camera the same distance in FRONT of
  the kart, looking back" — with the game's own FOV, near and far, and with a
  proper rotation, so winding (and therefore backface culling) is untouched.
  A left-handed "mirrored" basis would have inverted the winding and culled
  every visible face; the mirror CONVENTION is a U flip in the shell's plane
  shader instead.
- 2D output during the mirror pass goes to a small SINK framebuffer that is
  never published — the HUD framebuffer must not be touched after the eye
  passes published it, and it is sized to the eye extent, not the mirror's.
- The mirror pass restores mCurDimensions to the eye extent when it ends, so
  StartFrame's dims-changed framebuffer-resize sweep never sees the mirror
  size. Without that, alternating eye/mirror extents would re-resize every
  game framebuffer twice per host frame (the Ship of Harkinian port "black sky wedge").
VR R13 additions (rev7 — the four fixes the R13 scout maps named):
- item 1b: the eye-extent quiesce trigger now reads the extent the pass will
  ACTUALLY resize to, so a MIRROR extent change quiesces too. It read the eye
  extent before the eye==3 override reassigned it, which meant `vr set
  mirror_res` (and any eye change the mirror rounded differently) released the
  incumbent mirror texture with the compositor holding it raw.
- item 2a: the gate reservation is released for framebuffers that were gated
  and then NOT DRAWN — precisely on the no-command-buffer path, and by a
  per-frame age SWEEP in the shell for the ones that never reached
  mDrawnFramebuffers at all. One gSohVRWorldActive flip between the gate and
  Interpreter::Run leaked gate slot 2 permanently, and from the moment that
  texture became the published HUD every compositor claim was refused: the
  HUD stopped drawing for the rest of the session, silently.
- item 3: the sky's PITCH is re-keyed, per pass, by shifting its ortho
  projection's out[3][1] by the eye-vs-game-camera pitch difference. Only yaw
  was ever re-keyed; pitch has been open since R2.
- item 4: the rear pane's sky. R11's whole-ortho x-shift evacuated the
  yaw-INDEPENDENT gradient and floor along with the sprites; 0046 rev2's finer
  sentinels let the gradient and floor draw unshifted and the sprites drop.
REV15 (VR R18-A, ghost drivers round two): (a) THE BASE. The snapshot's eye
  matrices are composed by the compositor around the pose IT read; walks run on
  the game thread right after the export, so a walk can latch a matrix built
  from the PREVIOUS game frame's pose. R17-A's (prev - cur)(1 - t) assumed the
  base was always `cur`. Soh3DSeatLerp now adds (cur - seatBase), the shell
  publishing seatBase in new snapshot slots 24-27 (SOHVR_SKY_SLOTS 24 -> 28);
  `vr set seatrebase 0` is 1.0.0.16 exactly. Soh3DBaseProbe counts, in every
  arm, the walks whose base was not the current export. (b) THE CLASS PROBE
  (dev only, gSohVRClassProbe): G_NOOP 0x70/0x71 brackets from 0054 rev6 and
  0065 name an object class; the first modelview load inside is that class's
  drawn position, compared per walk with the eye recovered from the composed
  eye matrix ITSELF (x = y = w = 0) -- the instrument R17-A's probe was not,
  because it modelled the seat instead of reading it (trap D11).
REV16 (VR R21 item 2, the ghosts in the REAR-VIEW pane): the pane walk (eye
  index 3) never ran the seat's interpolation at all. It builds
  T = V_pane * V_game^-1 from the look-behind camera and the chase camera as
  0045 exported them for game frame N, and pre-multiplies it onto `in` -- the
  game's own view*projection, which FrameInterpolation has ALREADY moved to the
  walk's sub-frame t. So on every non-key walk the game eye inside `in` was not
  the eye T undid, and the residual went through T's rotation: for a 180-degree
  mirror it moved the pane camera FORWARD by the game camera's (1-t) step while
  every object was drawn at t -- D67's trap applied to T (the matrix built
  around one base, the content drawn at another). Soh3DPaneLerp moves T onto
  the walk: the look-behind camera to lerp(prev, cur, t) (0045 rev8 exports
  prev) and the game eye to the one `in` actually carries, read off the matrix
  itself (x = y = w = 0). It is the SAME correction the seat applies -- one
  walk weight (Soh3DWalkW) and one world pre-translation (Soh3DPreTranslate),
  shared, not copied. `vr set panelerp 0` = 1.0.1.19. The class probe gains a
  pane mode (`vr set classprobe 2`): the same table, sampled on the pane walk,
  with the eye recovered from the pane's composed matrix.
All new code is __IOS__-guarded; the shell globals live in SohIosShell.m
so iPhone links resolve (mode stays 0 there); macOS compiles none of it.

